Feature: Rank Products by Revenue and Evaluate Performance Consistency

  Background:
    Given the data is available in Unity Catalog at "purgo_playground.information_schema"
    And the dataset includes columns "product_type" and "purchased_date"

  Scenario Outline: Rank products by revenue for each country
    Given a dataset with product sales data spanning 12 months
    When I calculate total revenue for each <product_type> per country from <start_date> to <end_date>
    Then I rank products by revenue in descending order for each country

  Examples:
    | product_type | start_date | end_date   |
    | Electronics  | 2022-01-01 | 2022-12-31 |
    | Clothing     | 2022-01-01 | 2022-12-31 |

  Scenario Outline: Add performance column based on consistency criteria
    Given a ranked list of <product_type> for each month
    When I evaluate the number of months each product is in the top 3 rankings
    Then I classify <product_type> as Gold if ranked top 3 for >=6 months, Silver if >=3 and <6 months, Bronze if <3 months
    And I add this classification to a new column called "performance"

  Examples:
    | product_type |
    | Electronics  |
    | Clothing     |

  Scenario: Handle ties in rankings
    Given multiple products have identical revenues within a month for a specific country
    When calculating monthly ranks
    Then assign them equal rank positions without skipping subsequent ranks

  Scenario: Periodic recalculation of rankings based on new data
    Given new purchase data is added after initial ranking calculation 
    When recalculating rankings 
    Then update ranks and performance classifications based on latest complete set of data


